---
source: crates/vitrify-cli/tests/cli_help.rs
expression: "long_help(&cmd, &path)"
---
Print the procedure index, or the operative procedure for a task

Usage: vitrify brief [OPTIONS] [TASK]

Arguments:
  [TASK]
          The procedure to print (none: the index)

          Possible values:
          - onboard:    Take a repository from nothing to ready-to-build, or name the gaps
          - authoring:  A PRD to an Approved TDD and an Active, lint-clean SDD
          - change:     Change TDDs and SDDs, one or many, and record what each change stales
          - run:        Start, watch and read a `vitrify run` build
          - kickoff:    Drive the build loop from a session instead of `vitrify run`
          - build-unit: Build one unit (--unit --holder prints a worker's whole prompt)
          - integrate:  Take one built unit through the gate to Verified

Options:
      --unit <UNIT>
          Unit ID (build-unit worker-prompt generation)

      --holder <HOLDER>
          Holder identity (build-unit worker-prompt generation)

      --sdd <ROOT>
          SDD root for the worker prompt: a bundle directory, its sdd.md, or a single *.sdd.md (default: the one SDD in the repository)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Reads:   ~/.vitrify/briefs/<task>.md ($VITRIFY_HOME; an override on disk wins); build-unit
         with --unit --holder also reads the SDD, the unit's reading set and its claim
Writes:  nothing in the repository; restores or refreshes its copy under ~/.vitrify/
Prints:  no task: the procedure index (task, what it is for, who follows it)
         a task: that procedure, filled with this vitrify's version and values
         build-unit --unit --holder: the whole worker prompt vitrify run hands a worker
Exit status: 0 printed · 2 --unit and --holder not given together, or not to build-unit,
         or a usage error · 4 unknown unit, no SDD, or several and no --sdd
Config:  run.status_check_seconds (VITRIFY_RUN_STATUS_CHECK_SECONDS), in brief run;
         run.worktree_dir (VITRIFY_RUN_WORKTREE_DIR); run.lease_minutes
         (VITRIFY_RUN_LEASE_MINUTES), in the worker prompt; VITRIFY_HOME
Examples:
  vitrify brief
  vitrify brief change
  vitrify brief build-unit --unit U-003 --holder w1 --sdd specs/calc
